  "title": "eFPGA: The ASIC Power-Up, Not an Off-the-Shelf Substitute",
  "summary": "In semiconductor design, there is a persistent misconception that adding an embedded FPGA (eFPGA) to an SoC is simply a way to “shrink” a standalone FPGA onto your die. If you view eFPGA merely as a substitute for a Commercial Off-The-Shelf (COTS) FPGA, you’re overlooking its broader architectural and lifecycle advantages. From a Product Management [...]Read More... from eFPGA: The ASIC Power-Up, Not an Off-the-Shelf Substitute",
